  "body": "## Scope and evidence\n\n**Research consolidation; no new $\\kappa$.** Assigned by `scripts/choose_research_task.py` without rerolling (OS-random seed `a690c28b61e61a128b496b24d98aba3b`, track `consolidation`, task `overlap-receipt`, scope key `757723e3fd38f20fa774`), refined to Rohan Arun's (#211, head `c63e50a5dde96fe1459d6b29e55e47f42f104347`) complete 25-path / 13-direct-file source retention across incorporated #205, #210, and #217, Round-9 certificate reconciliation, and missing credit restoration in `CONTRIBUTORS.md`.\n\nAt base `0fdd7d82de03e43c9e5a1000dfbcd380d1b687d2`, `docs/research/pr-ledger.json` lists #211 as `partially_reviewed` with `integration_location: []` because #211 was in draft state when the `next100` batch (`#153\u2013#303`) selected 100 non-draft PRs\u2014even though #211 had already passed `complete-changed-work-replay-passed` at the exact same head in `research/community-round9-audit/review-ledger.json` and its 6,191 cascade-optimized frame bases were incorporated into 42+ downstream PRs (`#210`, `#216`, `#217`, `#221`, `#227`, ...), with zero mentions of #211 in `CONTRIBUTORS.md`.\n\n### What `research/pr211-retention-receipt` authenticates and reconciles\n\n1. **Complete 25-path / 13-direct-file Git tree and blob proof (`SOURCE-PROOF.json`, 41 raw Git objects):**\n   - **12 inherited #205 paths (`3b6b66891c..95c58706ad`):** All 11 files in `research/packed-diagonal-bit` (subtree `409a4737d6ca0aa6c59f40b732c5d4608e705246`) and `.github/workflows/packed-diagonal-bit.yml` (`b00ddc44b8f866f57a62a82dd7ba6b43894301b6`) are inherited unchanged from incorporated parent #205 (`95c58706ad231d532bd7038308946a0344d08186`, direct parent of `archive/pr-reconciliation-next100-20261013` `bd1b279e5e5449f81ca262c1647961e81dd69e50`).\n   - **13 direct #211 paths (`95c58706ad..c63e50a5dd`):** #211 adds `research/cascade-frames-bit` (subtree `1708e493cbb1931e4fd11eca058b72193dfec3ac`, 12 files) and `.github/workflows/cascade-frames-bit.yml` (`aed05819ec6a716b8de02d243b447031ef1309a1`):\n     - `opframe-bases.json` (4,977,602 B, Git blob `8433d7724cbed83401fa42beee8653c62657ec0d`, SHA256 `56b2ed0f6b867e8cafdc32ac70419cfda36d02838844572098b3fc77f8026e58`) is retained byte-identically in incorporated #210 (`b0c058ba979c748bb3a8604bfb6502e9fac9b84d:research/coordinated-crossover-pr200/search/pr211-frames.json`) and as gzip+base64 (`6b3b66eaa484a50f1f45ab9f7515a1b4ff26897f`) in incorporated #217 (`b739fc226a54a4a507989aa1bef092d491287451:research/butterfly-coordinated-bit-211/opframe-bases.json.gz.b64`), whose decompressed payload matches both digests identically.\n     - `NOTICE` (`9edc2572378be7a7819f229de985eeaffa1173b6`), `banks.py` (`6505ebd37e3414016168511cca7c2f69216cc9f1`), and `controls.py` (`51235415282f631caa4402e80b72f84915ff977d`) match their retained copies in #205 (and `NOTICE` is also retained in #210, #217, and `UPSTREAM-NOTICE`).\n     - All 9 remaining direct files (96,628 B total) are stored as authenticated raw Git blobs in `SOURCE-PROOF.json`.\n2. **Saved-certificate and child-histogram reconciliation (`verify.py`, `RESULT.json`):**\n   - Verifies all 6,191 replacement frame bases in `opframe-bases.json` (distinct operation indices in `0..40,265`, dimensions `3..21`, 65,501 total rows of length `h = 24`).\n   - Reconciles all 5 sections of `fresh` (`admitted`, `physical`, `arithmetic`, `independent`, `bank_controls`) in `research/community-round9-audit/pr211-changed.log.txt` against #211's `certificate.json` (`pinned_bit_files = 2,242`).\n   - Verifies the 34-sink terminal delta (`{\"3\": -102, \"21\": -102}`, rank reduction `2,448` from `1,486,160` to `1,483,712`), the internal/target physical histogram decomposition, the unpacked child-histogram delta `du` from #205 to #211 (`+531` children on internal ranks `1..19` in multiples of `3`, `0` rank-mass delta), and the 3-copy banked delta `dp = 3 * du` (`+1,593` children, `0` rank-mass delta at `W = 56,402`, `rank_mass = 4,055,136`, `deficit = 5,808`).\n   - Re-verifies the 3-level ordinary-leaf rational recurrence and balanced assembly grid ceiling (`\\kappa = 683847872495777/10^{18} > \\kappa_{\\text{PR207}} > \\kappa_{\\text{PR205}}$).\n3. **Attribution repair (`CONTRIBUTORS.md`):**\n   - Adds a concise credit paragraph for Rohan Arun's #211 alongside the existing #99/#1015 retention paragraphs without altering ledger dispositions or `certificates/selected-result.json`.\n\n## Reproduce\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/pr211-retention-receipt --check-only\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/pr211-retention-receipt\n```\n\nRuns the standalone offline checker (`PASS_PR211_RETENTION_AND_CERTIFICATE_RECONCILIATION paths=25 direct=13 frames=6191 child_delta=531 mass_delta=0`) and 19 unit tests (1 positive case + 18 corruption, coverage, provenance, frame-base, and accounting rejection controls) under `-I -O -B`.\n\n## Coordination and credit\n\n- **Coordination claim:** [Discussion #1166 comment](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1166#discussioncomment-18936472)\n- **Predecessor credit:** Rohan Arun (`@rohanarun`, #205/#211), `eumemic` (#168/#210), Henry Grant (`@hcg890`, #217), `Dugongue` (#207/#216/#227), Chafik Boukhalfa (`@chafreaky`, #200), Evan McKinney (`@evmckinney9`, #197), Avi Eisenberg (`@ikeboy`, #193), `maxime-fleury` (#204), `icekylinx` (#144/#184), and Douglas Colkitt (Round-9 and `next100` audits). Original notice preserved verbatim in `UPSTREAM-NOTICE`.\n- **Author & AI disclosure:** Prepared by steph4n (`@steph4n-gh`) with substantial Google Gemini assistance in investigation, implementation, verification, and writing. No independent human review claimed. Apache-2.0.",
